A cutscene is an animated sequence usually occurring during a quest in which a player has no control, and are often used to show the storyline of a certain quest. Cutscenes also occur during some transportation sequences such as charter ships, the eagle transport system and canoes.

During a cutscene, a player cannot talk, move, or click on most things to perform actions they can normally do, except examining objects or Non-player characters. Although in some cutscenes, the player will say something above their heads without typing it.

]]
The Air obelisk is located in level 7 Wilderness, and can be reached by climbing the ladder north of the Black demons in Edgeville Dungeon. It is used for enchanting unpowered orbs into air orbs (requires level 66 Magic), which costs 3 cosmic runes and 30 air runes per orb charge. This gives 76 Magic experience. At level 66 Crafting, an air orb can be attached to a battlestaff to make an air battlestaff, granting 137.5 Crafting experience.

As the Air obelisk is in the Wilderness, caution should be taken when visiting it due to player killing, and an unprepared charger can end up losing their orbs and runes. Bringing teleport items such as an amulet of glory or runes may be wise, although one still has to be careful, since players with a high Magic level may teleblock you.
